    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses ADR-030 by flipping status to Implemented, adding an Implementation section, and correcting ADR-029's mechanism prediction. **Documentation only — no code changes.**\n\n## Measured actuals exceeded predictions\n\nMeasured on Wikipedia at viewport 1774 after ADR-030 Commit 1:\n\n| Metric | ADR-029 baseline | Predicted | **Actual** | Delta vs prior |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `.mw-page-container-inner` y | 59 | 59 | **36** | **−23 (unexpected)** |\n| `.vector-page-toolbar` height | 687 | ~40-60 | **21** | **−666** |\n| `vector-body` (article) y | 834 | ~250-350 | **145** | **−689** |\n| `h1#firstHeading` y | 107 | 107 | **84** | **−23 (unexpected)** |\n\n**Article intro at y=145** — deeply above the fold, far better than the predicted ~250-350.\n\n### Two positive surprises documented\n\n1. **Toolbar collapsed to 21px** (not 40-60). The `.vector-page-toolbar-container` flex row + `font-size:var(--font-size-small,0.875rem)` produces a more compact result than expected.\n\n2. **The entire grid moved up 23px**. The `page-tools` flip also deactivates a companion rule under the `-disabled` state (`.mw-body { justify-content: center }`), freeing vertical space we didn't model. Not predicted — but consistent with the feature-class-flip mechanism (each flip can enable/disable multiple rules at once).\n\n## ADR-029's mechanism prediction corrected\n\nADR-029's Post-Implementation Note predicted:\n\n> \"A principled fix for `:checked` + `position: absolute` (ADR-030) will collapse the toolbar too and move the intro above the fold.\"\n\n**Wrong mechanism.** ADR-030's measurement showed the Tools panel was **not `:checked`-controlled** — it was another `vector-feature-*` flag on `<html>`. Same JS-set pattern as ADR-029's own main-menu flip. The visible bug was solved by the flip.\n\n`:checked` + `position: absolute` remain genuinely needed for future features (click-to-open dropdowns, infoboxes, thumbnails) and ADR-031 remains their home — but they weren't the mechanism behind the Tools panel.\n\n**This is now the third correction preserved in ADR-029's record:**\n1. Mid-cycle Commit 2 regression (motivated Commit 3)\n2. Post-merge language-dropdown overstatement (small workaround)\n3. This mechanism prediction (this PR)\n\nEach preserved in place rather than rewritten — same discipline as ADR-028's post-fix corrections to ADR-025/026/027.\n\n## Two honest deferrals in ADR-030\n\n1. **Infobox renders as inline list** (`.html` / `.htm` / `text/html` / `WHATWG` / `W3C` / … stacked at bottom of first viewport) instead of top-right `float: right` box. `float` not implemented. ADR-031 candidate or its own ADR.\n\n2. **Stray closing-tag fragment** in top-right of viewport. Parser leak, present in ADR-029 baseline too. Not introduced by ADR-030. Deferred to its own diagnostic.\n\nNeither regresses any prior ADR.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `docs/decisions/030-feature-class-extensions.md` — Status: Accepted → **Implemented**; new Implementation section (line 335, 114 lines) with actuals-vs-predictions table, two positive surprises explained, two honest deferrals documented, scope-reframe earned lesson\n- `docs/decisions/029-flex-layout.md` — new Post-ADR-030 update at line 496: corrects the mechanism prediction, records the third self-correction in ADR-029's cycle\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — new `### Added` entry for ADR-030 at top\n\n## What didn't change\n\n- Zero code changes\n- Test count unchanged: 399 cases / 1660 assertions\n- Full suite green\n- No behavior change to main\n\n## The arc's honesty pattern strengthened\n\nThree ADRs now carry explicit post-implementation corrections in their own records:\n\n| ADR | Corrections preserved |\n|---|---|\n| 025 | URL-fix post-correction (external CSS never actually loaded pre-ADR-028) |\n| 026 | Same as 025 |\n| 027 | Same as 025 |\n| 028 | Misdiagnosis correction (grid was correct; 585px header not grid bug) |\n| **029** | **Three corrections** — Commit 2 regression, language overstatement, mechanism prediction |\n| 030 | Actuals exceeded predictions (positive surprise, documented in place) |\n\nNone of these were rewrites. All preserved the original claim alongside the correction. That's the arc's actual contribution: a demonstrably honest historical record.\n\nRefs #166 #167\n",
